Mixture-model binarizer
-----------------------

Files:
    R/mixture_fit.R
    inst/stan/bimodal.stan
    inst/stan/bimodal_cv.stan
    inst/stan/unimodal.stan
    inst/stan/unimodal_cv.stan

These files adapt the mixture model, the Stan code (level1_ordered.stan,
level1_ordered_CV.stan, level1_unimodal.stan, level1_unimodal_CV.stan) and the
expression-calling logic of Fred P. Davis's opticlobe code:

    https://github.com/fredpdavis/opticlobe
    Copyright (c) 2018-2020 Fred P. Davis

published with

    Davis FP, Nern A, Picard S, et al. (2020). A genetic, genomic, and
    computational resource for exploring neural circuit function. eLife
    9:e50901. https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.50901

by way of the mm_marker / mixture_modeling_smk pipeline
(https://github.com/chenyenchung/mixture_modeling_smk).

The opticlobe repository carries no license. On 2026-10-26 Fred P. Davis gave
written permission (email to Yen-Chung Chen, archived by the maintainer) for
this adaptation and for its release under the MIT license. The adaptation is
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Yen-Chung Chen, and the whole is distributed under the
MIT license of scMarco.

Changes from opticlobe include a reimplementation in R around rstan and a fix
to the held-out elpd, which here averages each sample's likelihood over the
posterior draws (https://github.com/fredpdavis/opticlobe/pull/1).
